===== unravis audit =====
Compare API timings between two periods, from the running app

Usage:
  unravis audit [flags]
  unravis audit [command]

Available Commands:
  activity    Activity of the sources around a time, across their APIs and jobs (a live read, at most 24 hours)
  breakdown   Count the comparison's requests by status code, user, UI version, user agent, polling type or IP
  compare     Compare the timing of every API between a period and a baseline period
  groups      Page, search or sort the groups of the latest comparison (no new query on the sources)
  guide       Print the investigation guide of the audit tools
  requests    A page of the newest requests of one group (a live read of metadata)
  slowest     The slowest completed requests of the comparison (a live read of metadata)
  timeline    One group's timeline and baseline statistics (from the stored comparison)
  timelines   Compare the timelines of several groups

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for audit

Global Flags:
      --json                 same as -o json
      --no-color             no colour (there is none yet)
  -o, --output string        output format: table, json or jsonl (default "table")
      --output-file string   write JSON output to a new file (json mode only)
      --overwrite            with --output-file: replace an existing file
      --profile string       run as an automation profile (not available yet)
  -q, --quiet                no progress text on stderr
      --request string       the arguments of the operation as one JSON object, from a file or - for the input
      --timeout duration     give up after this long (at most 1h) (default 30s)

Use "unravis audit [command] --help" for more information about a command.
===== unravis audit activity =====
Activity of the sources around a time, across their APIs and jobs (a live read, at most 24 hours). Give the same arguments as one JSON object with --request FILE (or - for the input) to use every field of the tool ('unravis schema audit.activity' lists them).

Usage:
  unravis audit activity --source ID --start T --end T [flags]

Flags:
      --cursor string        the nextCursor of the last page
      --end string           end of the window (RFC 3339)
  -h, --help                 help for activity
      --limit int            rows on the page, 1 to 100
      --source stringArray   source id (repeat for more, 1 to 8)
      --start string         start of the window (RFC 3339)

Global Flags:
      --json                 same as -o json
      --no-color             no colour (there is none yet)
  -o, --output string        output format: table, json or jsonl (default "table")
      --output-file string   write JSON output to a new file (json mode only)
      --overwrite            with --output-file: replace an existing file
      --profile string       run as an automation profile (not available yet)
  -q, --quiet                no progress text on stderr
      --request string       the arguments of the operation as one JSON object, from a file or - for the input
      --timeout duration     give up after this long (at most 1h) (default 30s)
===== unravis audit breakdown =====
Count the comparison's requests by status code, user, UI version, user agent, polling type or IP. Give the same arguments as one JSON object with --request FILE (or - for the input) to use every field of the tool ('unravis schema audit.breakdown' lists them).

Usage:
  unravis audit breakdown --result-id ID --dim DIM [flags]

Flags:
      --dim string         statusCode, userId, uiVersion, userAgent, pollingType or userIp
  -h, --help               help for breakdown
      --include-ip         needed for --dim userIp (the app must allow identifiers)
      --result-id string   the result id that 'audit compare' printed
      --top int            values to list, 1 to 50 (0 or unset: 20)

Global Flags:
      --json                 same as -o json
      --no-color             no colour (there is none yet)
  -o, --output string        output format: table, json or jsonl (default "table")
      --output-file string   write JSON output to a new file (json mode only)
      --overwrite            with --output-file: replace an existing file
      --profile string       run as an automation profile (not available yet)
  -q, --quiet                no progress text on stderr
      --request string       the arguments of the operation as one JSON object, from a file or - for the input
      --timeout duration     give up after this long (at most 1h) (default 30s)
===== unravis audit compare =====
Runs one comparison on the running app and prints the groups that slowed down most. The result id it prints keeps the result in the app for ten minutes: use 'unravis audit groups --result-id ID' to page or filter it with no second query on the sources.

Times are RFC 3339 with an explicit zone, for example 2026-11-23T09:00:00Z. Give the same arguments as one JSON object with --request FILE (or - for the input) to use every field of the tool ('unravis schema audit.compare' lists them). A comparison can take five minutes.

Usage:
  unravis audit compare --source ID --start T --end T --baseline-start T --baseline-end T [flags]

Flags:
      --action string                only this action or job method
      --audit-id string              only this audit record id (24 hex characters)
      --baseline-end string          end of the baseline period (RFC 3339)
      --baseline-start string        start of the baseline period (RFC 3339)
      --bucket-seconds int           width of a chart slot, 10 to 86400 (default 60)
      --completion string            completion: all, complete, incomplete, pending, invalid
      --controller string            only this controller or job type
      --end string                   end of the period (RFC 3339)
  -h, --help                         help for compare
      --kind string                  request kind: all, synchronous, asynchronous, hangfire, http, http_unknown (default "all")
      --limit int                    groups on the first page, 1 to 100 (default 20)
      --metric string                timing: total or api (default "total")
      --operation string             only this Controller.Action
      --outcome string               outcome: all, success, failure, client_error, server_error (default "all")
      --sort string                  order: p95_delta_ms, p95_ratio or current_count
      --source stringArray           source id (repeat for more, 1 to 8)
      --start string                 start of the period (RFC 3339)
      --status-code stringArray      only this status code (repeat)
      --ui-version stringArray       only this UI version (repeat)
      --url-contains string          only URLs that contain this text
      --user-agent-contains string   only user agents that contain this text
      --user-id stringArray          only this user id (repeat)
      --user-ip stringArray          only this IP address (repeat)

Global Flags:
      --json                 same as -o json
      --no-color             no colour (there is none yet)
  -o, --output string        output format: table, json or jsonl (default "table")
      --output-file string   write JSON output to a new file (json mode only)
      --overwrite            with --output-file: replace an existing file
      --profile string       run as an automation profile (not available yet)
  -q, --quiet                no progress text on stderr
      --request string       the arguments of the operation as one JSON object, from a file or - for the input
      --timeout duration     give up after this long (at most 1h) (default 30s)
===== unravis audit groups =====
Page, search or sort the groups of the latest comparison (no new query on the sources)

Usage:
  unravis audit groups --result-id ID [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help               help for groups
      --limit int          groups to show, 1 to 100 (default 20)
      --offset int         first group to show
      --result-id string   the result id that 'audit compare' printed
      --search string      only groups whose controller, action, source, type or outcome contains this text
      --sort string        order: p95_delta_ms, p95_ratio or current_count
      --state string       only groups in this state: compared, missing_current, missing_reference, insufficient_data, undefined_baseline

Global Flags:
      --json                 same as -o json
      --no-color             no colour (there is none yet)
  -o, --output string        output format: table, json or jsonl (default "table")
      --output-file string   write JSON output to a new file (json mode only)
      --overwrite            with --output-file: replace an existing file
      --profile string       run as an automation profile (not available yet)
  -q, --quiet                no progress text on stderr
      --request string       the arguments of the operation as one JSON object, from a file or - for the input
      --timeout duration     give up after this long (at most 1h) (default 30s)
