===== unravis audit requests =====
A page of the newest requests of one group (a live read of metadata). Give the same arguments as one JSON object with --request FILE (or - for the input) to use every field of the tool ('unravis schema audit.requests' lists them). With -o jsonl it prints one line per row, page after page, up to --max-rows (1000 unless set) and 64 MiB; --limit is then the page size. A stream that stops at a limit ends with coverage partial and the nextCursor to continue from.

Usage:
  unravis audit requests --result-id ID --api-key KEY [flags]

Flags:
      --api-key string     the exact group key from 'audit compare' or 'audit groups' (never rebuild it from names)
      --cursor string      the nextCursor of the last page
  -h, --help               help for requests
      --limit int          rows on the page, 1 to 100
      --max-bytes int      with -o jsonl: most bytes to print, at most 64 MiB (default 67108864)
      --max-rows int       with -o jsonl: most rows to print, 1 to 10000 (default 1000)
      --result-id string   the result id that 'audit compare' printed

Global Flags:
      --json                 same as -o json
      --no-color             no colour (there is none yet)
  -o, --output string        output format: table, json or jsonl (default "table")
      --output-file string   write JSON output to a new file (json mode only)
      --overwrite            with --output-file: replace an existing file
      --profile string       run as an automation profile (not available yet)
  -q, --quiet                no progress text on stderr
      --request string       the arguments of the operation as one JSON object, from a file or - for the input
      --timeout duration     give up after this long (at most 1h) (default 30s)
===== unravis audit slowest =====
The slowest completed requests of the comparison (a live read of metadata). Give the same arguments as one JSON object with --request FILE (or - for the input) to use every field of the tool ('unravis schema audit.slowest' lists them). With -o jsonl it prints one line per row, page after page, up to --max-rows (1000 unless set) and 64 MiB; --limit is then the page size. A stream that stops at a limit ends with coverage partial and the nextCursor to continue from.

Usage:
  unravis audit slowest --result-id ID [flags]

Flags:
      --cursor string      the nextCursor of the last page
  -h, --help               help for slowest
      --limit int          rows on the page, 1 to 50
      --max-bytes int      with -o jsonl: most bytes to print, at most 64 MiB (default 67108864)
      --max-rows int       with -o jsonl: most rows to print, 1 to 10000 (default 1000)
      --min-ms float       only requests at least this slow, in milliseconds
      --result-id string   the result id that 'audit compare' printed

Global Flags:
      --json                 same as -o json
      --no-color             no colour (there is none yet)
  -o, --output string        output format: table, json or jsonl (default "table")
      --output-file string   write JSON output to a new file (json mode only)
      --overwrite            with --output-file: replace an existing file
      --profile string       run as an automation profile (not available yet)
  -q, --quiet                no progress text on stderr
      --request string       the arguments of the operation as one JSON object, from a file or - for the input
      --timeout duration     give up after this long (at most 1h) (default 30s)
